## Giving Smart Hints for Guesses

A good hint system doesn't just say 'wrong' — it tells you which direction to go and whether you're getting warmer.

### Basic Hints: High, Low, or Correct

```xiom
fn check_guess(secret: Int, guess_str: Str) -> Result[Str, Str] {
  let guess = string.str_to_int(guess_str);

  let g = match guess {
    Ok(n) => n,
    Err(_) => { return Err("That's not a number!"); }
  };

  if g == secret {
    return Ok("Correct! You found it!");
  }
  elif g > secret {
    return Ok("Too high! Try lower.");
  }
  else {
    return Ok("Too low! Try higher.");
  }
}
```

### Adding Distance Hints

Now let's add proximity — is the player close?

```xiom
fn check_guess_detailed(secret: Int, guess_str: Str) -> Result[Str, Str] {
  let guess = string.str_to_int(guess_str);

  let g = match guess {
    Ok(n) => n,
    Err(_) => { return Err("That's not a number!"); }
  };

  let diff = g - secret;
  if diff < 0 { diff = -diff; }

  if g == secret {
    return Ok("Correct! You found it!");
  }
  elif diff <= 2 {
    if g > secret { return Ok("Very close! Too high."); }
    else { return Ok("Very close! Too low."); }
  }
  elif diff <= 10 {
    if g > secret { return Ok("Warm. Too high."); }
    else { return Ok("Warm. Too low."); }
  }
  else {
    if g > secret { return Ok("Too high!"); }
    else { return Ok("Too low!"); }
  }
}
```

### The Game Loop Pattern

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let secret = 42;

  match check_guess_detailed(secret, "40") {
    Ok(hint) => { io.println(hint); }
    Err(e) => { io.println(e); }
  }

  match check_guess_detailed(secret, "42") {
    Ok(hint) => { io.println(hint); }
    Err(e) => { io.println(e); }
  }

  match check_guess_detailed(secret, "99") {
    Ok(hint) => { io.println(hint); }
    Err(e) => { io.println(e); }
  }

  return 0;
}
```

